      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Rationalize the denominator of $\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{ab}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the quotient rule and put the numerator and denominator under separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{ab}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{ab}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to remove the radical $\\sqrt{ab}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{ab},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{ab}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{ab}}{\\sqrt{ab}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2ab}}{(\\sqrt{ab})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2ab}}{ab}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
